  "summary": "The quiz leaderboard is now four leaderboards — today's, this week's, this month's and the all-time one — each of every quiz or of one category (a quiz of the catalog). The learner chooses the period with a segmented choice on the leaderboard page and on the centre card of the overview and the category with a second one on the page; every column heading of both tables is a button that sorts by its column and turns the order around on a second click. A period is a calendar window in UTC around the proctor's clock (day, ISO week from Monday, month); the proctor ranks every board itself from one transcript per learner (submitted runs and badges) with a compact rank index per asked period and quiz, answers one board per query with its window, and counts the submissions of the whole catalog so the client knows when to refresh the crowds. Contract, both cores, the Python reference, the vectors, the proctor, the React client, the site's Playwright spec and the documentation moved together. See 📓️design.md for the decisions and 📓️report.md for what changed and what was verified; the six end-to-end failures left in the results screen at close belong to the concurrent results and crowd rework, and the capacity gate and the rehearsal topology were not run.",
